From 5cd92ba52a4fbbb83446ad877b1b179abfe12b43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:24:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: add logfmt as a built-in output format

Render typed event fields and core metadata on the logger thread. Quote string values with JSON-compatible escapes so quotes, controls and malformed UTF-8 cannot create extra records; retain numeric and boolean values. Keep text as the default and use bare source function names.

Validation: 29 logging/event cases pass; feature_logging starts, mines and shuts down a node with the real logfmt file sink. All 209 records from that sink also decode with upstream go-logfmt v0.6.0. Full inherited baseline was run separately before this change; its four async log-wait failures are repaired in the preceding fixup. Linux collector and cloud ingestion checks are not claimed.
(cherry picked from commit ed491a6bcdab784d2910a8949138cb81f791a094)

